{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785183896,"nonce":"rmKkvQxnVaSqPh26hStc4l9kjHg=","title":"ADR-0062 s8: reap Farms and Exports, and give the warm tier a space bound","message":"Farms and Exports are directories on a bounded disk. Today the warm tier has **no eviction at all**. ADR-0062 moves this from a nice-to-have onto the critical path: without it the service fills its volume and stops.\n\nFarms are LRU-evictable cache objects keyed by snapshot root (a miss is slower, never wrong). Exports are per-Attempt and must be reaped when the Attempt settles — a leaked Export is a leaked directory **and a leaked capability**.\n\nSupersedes/absorbs the pre-existing warm-tier LRU ticket `24476bc`, including its finding that `list_objects` gives last-*written* rather than last-*read*, which is the wrong key for immutable content.\n\n\n- [ ] A space bound is enforced and eviction is by least-recently-*used*, not least-recently-written\n- [ ] Evicting a Farm that a live Export still uses as its lower layer is impossible\n- [ ] Exports are reaped on settle, on Attempt abandonment, and on service restart (orphan sweep)\n- [ ] Reaping a leaked Export also revokes its capability\n- [ ] Eviction never breaks a promise: cold retention is the guarantee, warm promises nothing (ADR-0061 retention table)\n\n\n- 873d301 (s1), s4","files":null}]}